H8/300 (h8300) test binaries
============================

GCC-built ELF binaries for the Hitachi H8/300 architecture (normal mode,
16-bit), used as reproduction cases for rizin h8300 analysis issues
(#6794 stackframe annotation gap, #6795 rz_analysis_mask heap overflow).

Files
-----

* `main.elf` — small multi-function C program compiled with debug info
  (DWARF). sha256 `121bc56ec4a7326e80139dd536e5ca99c11d04d40f90d2d0b236e992109bf3cd`
* `main-nodebug.elf` — same program without debug info.
  sha256 `8891b8c2a2b24adb2c2fe0d2cee9b2a93008c8813d9f972357e0e32f9ad47353`
* `emulateme.c` — the C source both binaries were built from.

Rebuild
-------

With an h8300 GCC toolchain (exact original flags not recorded; the debug
binary contains DWARF from a `-g` build of the source, approximate):

    h8300-elf-gcc -g -O0 -o main.elf emulateme.c
    h8300-elf-gcc -O0 -o main-nodebug.elf emulateme.c

Reproduction notes
------------------

    rizin -q -c 'ao @ 0x534' main.elf      # aborts: heap overflow (#6795)
    rizin -q -c 'ao @ 0x47e' main.elf      # fine (control)
    rizin -A -q -c 'afi @ dbg.main~stackframe' main.elf
                                           # reports 8, ISA truth is 12 (#6794)
